      "reasoning": "Article 8(2)(e)(vi) lists \"Committing rape, sexual slavery, ...\" as a serious violation applicable to non‑international armed conflicts. The provision does not condition liability on the victim’s status; it criminalises the act itself. Accordingly, when members of the UPC/FPLC are subjected to rape or sexual slavery by fellow members, the conduct falls squarely within the definition of a war crime.",
